# Single pinned toolchain source of truth.
#
# docs/00_README.md (Toolchain lifecycle) requires the exact selected versions to be
# recorded in the G1 evidence and requires CI to fail on toolchain drift. This file is
# that record. scripts/verify_toolchain.py fails the build if any manifest in the
# repository disagrees with these values, so drift cannot reach a protected branch.
#
# Selection rule applied (docs/00): the latest stable release that is still
# security-supported at bootstrap. Security patches are reviewed monthly; critical/high
# fixes land within 14 days; routine supported patch updates land quarterly. A
# major-version upgrade requires compatibility tests, migration notes, and an approved ADR
# when behavior or operational assumptions change.
#
# Deviation: ESLINT_VERSION is 9.39.5 rather than the latest 10.11.0. See RISK-11 in
# .kilo/ecc/project-brain/risks.md and EV-013. The value is declared here so the drift
# gate tracks the pin, and the exception stays visible instead of being buried in
# package.json.

GO_VERSION=1.26.2
NODE_VERSION=24.18.0
PYTHON_VERSION=3.14.6

# Not enforced by the drift gate: ESLint is pinned in apps/web/package.json only.
# Declared here for visibility, and asserted by tests/ci/test_toolchain_gate.py.
ESLINT_VERSION=9.39.5

# Container base images are pinned to an exact patch tag, never a floating tag. Verified
# to exist in the official library/postgres registry on 2026-09-28; 17.11 is the current
# 17.x release, per the latest-security-supported selection rule in docs/00.
# Digest-level pinning is additionally performed by the SBOM/provenance job.
POSTGRES_IMAGE=postgres:17.11-alpine
